From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 07:29:06 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] v3dv: size explicitly laid out planes from their own offset

v3d_setup_plane_slices() takes a plane's start from the explicit plane
layout when one is given, but computes the plane's size as its end minus
plane_offset, the running sum of the sizes of the planes before it. That
is only right when the layout puts the planes one after the other in
plane order. A layout whose planes are in another order makes the uint32
subtraction wrap, the image's size goes past 4 GiB and vkCreateImage
fails with VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DEVICE_MEMORY.

Android hits it with every software-decoded video frame under Venus: a
YV12 buffer has its planes in memory as Y, Cr, Cb, Vulkan's
G8_B8_R8_3PLANE_420 orders them Y, Cb, Cr, and the guest driver passes
the Android buffer's offsets in Vulkan's plane order, so Cr's offset is
below Cb's. The AHardwareBuffer import fails and SurfaceFlinger aborts
("Failed to create a valid texture ... format:842094169"), measured on a
Raspberry Pi 5 host on 2026-10-14.

Count each plane's size from where the plane starts, and make the image
end where its last-ending plane does. Without an explicit layout the
planes follow each other, and both are what they were. A disjoint plane
has memory of its own, which has to hold the layout's offset as well, so
its size still counts from 0, as before.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/src/broadcom/vulkan/v3dv_image.c
+++ b/src/broadcom/vulkan/v3dv_image.c
@@ -101,7 +101,7 @@ v3d_get_dimension_mpad(uint32_t dimension, uint32_t level, uint32_t block_dimens
 
 static bool
 v3d_setup_plane_slices(struct v3dv_device *device, struct v3dv_image *image,
-                       uint8_t plane, uint32_t plane_offset,
+                       uint8_t plane, uint32_t plane_offset, bool disjoint,
                        const VkSubresourceLayout *plane_layouts)
 {
    assert(image->planes[plane].cpp > 0);
@@ -156,6 +156,12 @@ v3d_setup_plane_slices(struct v3dv_device *device, struct v3dv_image *image,
       offset = plane_offset;
    }
    assert(plane_offset % 64 == 0);
+   /* where this plane starts: with an explicit layout its offset need not
+    * follow the planes before it (Android's YV12 puts Cr before Cb, which
+    * Vulkan's plane order reverses), so the plane's size is counted from
+    * here, not from plane_offset. A disjoint plane has its own memory, which
+    * must hold the layout's offset too, so its size still counts from 0. */
+   const uint32_t plane_start = plane_layouts && !disjoint ? offset : plane_offset;
 
    for (int32_t i = image->vk.mip_levels - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
       struct v3d_resource_slice *slice = &image->planes[plane].slices[i];
@@ -277,7 +283,7 @@ v3d_setup_plane_slices(struct v3dv_device *device, struct v3dv_image *image,
       offset += slice_total_size;
    }
 
-   image->planes[plane].size = offset - plane_offset;
+   image->planes[plane].size = offset - plane_start;
 
    /* UIF/UBLINEAR levels need to be aligned to UIF-blocks, and LT only
     * needs to be aligned to utile boundaries.  Since tiles are laid out
@@ -354,11 +360,18 @@ v3d_setup_slices(struct v3dv_device *device, struct v3dv_image *image,
    uint64_t offset = 0;
    for (uint8_t plane = 0; plane < image->plane_count; plane++) {
       offset = disjoint ? 0 : offset;
-      if (!v3d_setup_plane_slices(device, image, plane, offset, plane_layouts)) {
+      if (!v3d_setup_plane_slices(device, image, plane, offset, disjoint,
+                                  plane_layouts)) {
          assert(plane_layouts);
          return VK_ERROR_INVALID_DRM_FORMAT_MODIFIER_PLANE_LAYOUT_EXT;
       }
-      offset += align64(image->planes[plane].size, 64);
+      /* the image ends where its last-ending plane does; without an explicit
+       * layout the planes follow each other and that is the running sum (a
+       * disjoint plane's size already counts from 0) */
+      const uint64_t plane_end =
+         (plane_layouts && !disjoint ? plane_layouts[plane].offset : offset) +
+         align64(image->planes[plane].size, 64);
+      offset = MAX2(offset, plane_end);
    }
 
    /* From the Vulkan spec:
